Usage: deq leet [<text>] [options]

Write text with Deq glyphs (Deq Leet), or read it back with --decode.

Arguments:
  [<text>]  Latin, Kurmanji or Sorani text, at most 1024 characters.

Options:
      --decode <file>          Print the text of a Deq Leet SVG written at the
                               basic level; pass the render flags used to write
                               it.
      --level <level>          basic is readable and decodable, advanced mixes
                               in seeded alternatives, full uses motifs. Default
                               basic. Values: basic, advanced, full.
      --script <script>        Glyph table. Default sorani for Arabic-script
                               text, else latin. Values: latin, sorani.
      --seed <n>               Seed for the advanced level, 0 to 4294967295.
                               Default 1.
      --letter-spacing <n>     Space between glyphs in grid units, 0 to 24.
                               Default 2.
      --line-spacing <n>       Space between lines in grid units, 0 to 48.
                               Default 6.
      --align <align>          Line alignment; start is the right edge for
                               Sorani. Default start. Values: start, center,
                               end.
      --format <format>        Output format. Default svg. Values: svg, png,
                               jpg, webp.
      --size <px>              Size in px of one 24 x 24 cell, 1 to 8192.
                               Default 24.
      --colors <list>          Comma-separated colours given to the glyphs in
                               turn (1 to 16).
      --title <text>           Accessible title. Default the normalised text; ""
                               marks the image decorative.
      --out <path>             Output file or directory; - writes to stdout.
                               Default: the current directory.
      --color <color>          Stroke and dot colour (any CSS colour). Default
                               currentColor.
      --stroke-width <n>       Stroke width in grid units, 0.05 to 12. Default
                               2.
      --absolute-stroke-width  Keep the stroke the same width in px at any size.
      --fill <color>           Fill for closed outlines, or none. Default none.
      --fill-opacity <0-1>     Opacity of the fill. Default 1.
      --stroke-opacity <0-1>   Opacity of strokes and dots. Default 1.
      --linecap <linecap>      Line ends. Default round. Values: round, butt,
                               square.
      --linejoin <linejoin>    Line corners. Default round. Values: round,
                               miter, bevel.
      --dot-scale <n>          Multiply every dot radius, 0.1 to 4. Default 1.
      --padding <n>            Space around the 24 x 24 canvas in grid units, 0
                               to 24. Default 0.
      --background <color>     Background colour, or none. Default none.
      --current-color <color>  What currentColor means in PDF and image formats.
                               Default black.
      --matte <color>          JPG background behind transparent pixels. Default
                               white.
      --quality <0-100>        JPG and WebP quality. Default 90.
      --force                  Overwrite existing files.
  -h, --help                   Show help.
  -V, --version                Print the version.
